IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nccp-borrower`

-- National Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009 (Cth) and the National Credit Code (Schedule 1), with the National Consumer
-- Credit Protection Regulations 2010 -- worked cases from the seat of the borrower.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case. The ASIC instrument under s 160F is not deposited.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad
-- gen_national-consumer-credit-protection-act-2009_baseline.py). Expected results were written by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-*): Chloe, 21, on a $70,000 graduate salary, gets a
-- credit card on 10 June 2024 (c043); Chloe and Liam settle a Byford house-and-land package with a mortgage on 15 May 2028
-- (c052); Jake, 24, takes two credit cards on 2 March 2031 (k048); takes "a $2,000 small-amount loan at the capped charges"
-- on 20 August 2032 (k049; the scenario's question list has "$400 a month on $2,000"); and on 22 August 2036 a friend's debt
-- to an unlicensed lender is brought to his door as paint and glue (k063).
-- The scenarios give no card limits, loan terms, assessment dates, incomes per repayment period, defaults or hardship; the
-- figures used for them below are the encoder's. The defaults and hardship notices are variants, not events of the lives.

`k063: the unlicensed lender to Jake's friend` MEANS `Lender or collector` WITH
    `is the credit provider under my credit contract` IS TRUE
    `carries on a business of providing credit to which the Code applies` IS TRUE
    `exercises a credit provider's rights against me, for itself or on its behalf` IS FALSE
    `holds a licence authorising the activity` IS FALSE
    `acts within authority as employee, director or credit representative of a licensed principal` IS FALSE
    `acts within authority as representative of a principal exempted under s 109 or s 110` IS FALSE

`k063: the man who glued the lock, collecting for that lender` MEANS `Lender or collector` WITH
